# The repo stores and checks out text as LF on every platform.
#
# This is load-bearing, not cosmetic: packages/space commits a generated
# sin-lut.ts and its test asserts the file is byte-identical to what the
# generator produces. Without this, a checkout under core.autocrlf=true
# rewrites the committed LF file to CRLF, the generator still emits LF, and
# the determinism check fails for reasons that have nothing to do with the
# LUT. Golden-file comparisons elsewhere are exposed to the same hazard.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.glb binary
*.wav binary
*.onnx binary
